.Sh DESCRIPTION
The RC5 encryption algorithm for EVP.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_rc5_32_12_16_cbc(), EVP_rc5_32_12_16_cfb(), EVP_rc5_32_12_16_cfb64(), EVP_rc5_32_12_16_ecb(), EVP_rc5_32_12_16_ofb()
RC5 encryption algorithm in CBC, CFB, ECB and OFB modes respectively.
This is a variable key length cipher with an additional "number of
rounds" parameter.
By default the key length is set to 128 bits and 12 rounds.
Alternative key lengths can be set using
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_set_key_length 3 .
The maximum key length is 2040 bits.
.Pp
The following rc5 specific
.Em ctrl Ns s
are supported (see
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl 3 Ns ).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl(ctx, EVP_CTRL_SET_RC5_ROUNDS, rounds, NULL)
Sets the number of rounds to
.Sy rounds .
This must be one of RC5_8_ROUNDS, RC5_12_ROUNDS or RC5_16_ROUNDS.
.It EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl(ctx, EVP_CTRL_GET_RC5_ROUNDS, 0, &rounds)
Stores the number of rounds currently configured in
.Sy *rounds
where
.Sy *rounds
is an int.
.El
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling these functions multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_CIPHER-RC5 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return an
.Sy EVP_CIPHER
structure that contains the implementation of the symmetric cipher.
See
.Xr EVP_CIPHER_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_CIPHER
structure.
